// Kestrel-RT Phase 2 ESP32-S3 firmware: a fork of the official Arduino UNO R4 WiFi USB bridge 0.5.2
// (github.com/arduino/uno-r4-wifi-usb-bridge, tag 0.5.2, UNOR4USBBridge.ino).
//
// Kept from upstream, unchanged in behavior:
//   - USB identity 2341:1002, CMSIS-DAP (HID) with the 0xAA feature report -> ESP ROM download mode
//   - USB CDC <-> UART0 (GPIO44/43) bridge to the RA4M1 SCI9 at the host's baud rate
//   - CDC line-coding 1200 (RA4 double reset into its bootloader) and 2400 (RA4 ROM boot mode)
// Changed:
//   - RA4 RESET (GPIO4) and MD/BOOT (GPIO9) are driven HIGH before they become outputs (upstream made
//     them outputs first, which pulsed RA4 RESET low on every ESP boot and reset the RA4M1).
//   - the AT-command server on UART1 (GPIO6 RX / GPIO5 TX) is replaced by the Kestrel mailbox node
//     (kx_node.cpp): framed, sequenced, CRC-checked protocol at 1,000,000 baud, Wi-Fi SoftAP, UDP.
// The ESP32-S3 is the untrusted domain: nothing here can change RA4 timing, priorities or code.
.
